{
  "case_id": "2012-12-62",
  "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen B. Kinnaird",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sentencing Petitioner Marvin Peugh, the district court applied the 2009 guidelines sentencing range of 70 to 87 months, rather than the 1998 range of 37 to 46 months applicable at the time of his offense. Retroactive application of harsher guidelines passed after the offense violates the Ex Post Facto Clause if it -- if it creates a significant risk of increased punishment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me. A mandatory schedule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that what your definition of legal consequence is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen B. Kinnaird",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The legal consequence is the -- is the ultimate sentence imposed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the statutes allowing relatives and friends of the victim to testify? Let's assume a crime committed before -- a horrible crime committed before that statute is enacted. Does it violate the ex post facto law to give effect to that statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen B. Kinnaird",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The guidelines are distinctive because they are the actual benchmark, and they must -- and the starting point for any sentencing. It is critical at what range you start your sentencing analysis, it's going to affect the analysis, whether you're starting at a range of 20 to 30 months or 120 --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But saying that the sentencer has to consider testimony from the victim or from relatives of the deceased, that -- that change in sentencing law is okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is evidence brought before the sentencer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're answering me differently now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I'm asking you to draw it. So tell me, what's the rule? Do you want something as broad that says even that kind of change can be an ex post facto? And, if you don't, articulate how I draw the line."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would have thought you would have gone back to Calder and Bull."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. Then rely on Garner, but not on Calder v. Bull."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We opposed certiorari largely on that ground. We don't think the guidelines impose a constraint on a district court's exercise of sentencing discretion; that is, if a judge decides that a guidelines range that the Commission has suggested at some other time suggests a more appropriate sentence or if the judge believes that some sentence that's unrelated to any guidelines range is the most appropriate sentence, the judge has discretion to impose that sentence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin (Government)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government changed its position in response to this Court's decisions in Gall, Kimbrough, and Irizarry because, before those decisions came out, there was an argument that the guidelines still imposed some substantive legal constraint on a district court's sentencing discretion. After Gall, Kimbrough, and Irizarry, after Nelson and Spears, that argument no longer exists."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The guidelines range gets a presumption of reasonableness at the appellate level."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0012",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question is whether it inflicts greater punishment. And there is a test on that, and the controlling inquiry is whether retroactive application of a change in a law that affects punishment created a sufficient risk of increasing the measure of punishment attached."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I assume that the statute is one that permits 10 days, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, there are two complaints that Petitioner could be making about his particular sentencing. One could be that he thinks the judge treated the guidelines too deferentially as a legal matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He's saying that -- the question is which guidelines in this case? And he's saying it's the guidelines in effect at the time he committed the crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, Petitioner argued in this case that the former guidelines range suggested a more appropriate sentence than the 2009 guidelines range."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court considered that argument, and it rejected it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is reversible error, is it not, simply to blindly apply the guidelines without considering the factors in 3553? That's reversible, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, surely, you do not want judges living in a world where they think that they cannot give deference to the guidelines, isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How would a court go about answering that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen B. Kinnaird",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF STEPHEN B. KINNAIRD ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-62",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9777734eaa3c7da01e7fb7e83448d1f529a421d3e4df9d812fa503cc76067214",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9777734eaa3c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:09 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
